module noRecursiveAdt

-- LIMIT: `data` declares NULLARY finite enums only — every constructor is a
--   bare tag carrying no payload (and enums erase to `Nat`). So you cannot
--   declare a recursive or parametric datatype: no user-defined `Tree`, no
--   user-defined `List`. `Node Tree Tree` below has no place to put its fields.
-- EXPECTED: parse/compile error at the payload constructor.
-- OBSERVED: a parse error at the payload -- "unexpected 'T'  /  expecting ':'"
--   (the parser reads `Leaf` and `Node` as tags, then has nowhere to put the
--    `Tree` fields, so it demands the `:` of the next declaration.)
-- FIX: see the commented workaround below the faulty code.

data Tree = Leaf | Node Tree Tree

-- WORKAROUND (compiles): the built-ins cover what `data` cannot —
-- data Shape = Circle | Square    -- nullary enum is fine
-- type Pair = Nat * Nat           -- record via a product alias
-- a runtime-recursive collection is `List Nat` (or `Text`); a two-way choice
-- is the built-in sum `Nat + Text`, taken apart with `left` / `right`.
